==Finnish==
{{Finnish index|k|u}}

===Etymology===
Possibly from {{proto|urj-pro|kumpa|wave|lang=fi}}, whence also eg. Hungarian {{term|hab||foam|lang=hu}}. {{etyl|gem|fi}} origin is also possible, cf. {{proto|gem-pro|humpaz|lang=}} (whence English {{term|hump}}).

===Noun===
{{fi-noun}}

# A [[hummock]], [[hillock]] (small natural elevation of earth, generally smaller than {{term|kukkula||hill}}, larger than {{term|kumpare||knoll}}).
# A [[mound]] (small, rounded, artificial elevation of earth).

